## Protocol Boundary

The external operator is storage, not truth. It signs each snapshot so transport
or cache corruption is detectable, but the verifier does not trust its claimed
tree root. The snapshot contains the complete bounded journal. The verifier
replays the journal, parses every canonical leaf, recomputes every predecessor
root and current root, and checks the frame-9015 predecessor chain carried by
the leaves. With at most 64 leaves this materialized proof is intentionally
larger and simpler to audit than a compact consistency path.

The fixed Witness Mesh v1 council signs the journal coordinate after each
append. An epoch becomes quorum-witnessed only when at least three members have
retained the same coordinate; one or two partial receipts do not advance the
committed boundary. A fresh strong read queries the witnesses directly and
requires at least three last-retained statuses matching the operator's exact
journal count and head. A single operator can serve an old or forked signed
snapshot, but cannot make it match a different fresh 3-of-4 checkpoint without
an honest witness changing or equivocating on its retained coordinate, or a
signature forgery. Three witnesses may still lag together at the previous
quorum-witnessed coordinate while a new append is only partially anchored; the
new epoch is not strong in that window and recovery must finish its anchor.
This is split-view detection under the existing `n=4`, `q=3`, `f<=1`
honest-intersection assumption, not a new consensus protocol.

Only the accepted active leaf must be the latest leaf. Epoch one is the
empty-tree bootstrap state. For transition `e -> e+1`, its one-based index is
`e`, its predecessor tree size is `e-1`, and the current tree size is `e`.
Accepting an older included leaf as active would make rollback
indistinguishable from history membership, so frame 9016 requires the active
index to equal the current tree size and `to_epoch = tree_size + 1`.

## Crash Semantics

The log append precedes witness anchoring, and witness anchoring precedes the
strong active receipt. If the client crashes after append, retry reuses the
literal leaf returned by the operator rather than reconstructing it against the
already-advanced tree. A different returned leaf refuses rather than being
reconstructed or accepted. If it crashes after anchoring, the mesh recovery path
reuses the current receipts. If it crashes after the strong active rename,
retry is idempotent. No intermediate state is accepted by the strong verifier.

The legacy frame-9015 active pointer remains available for compatibility. It is
not cross-host rollback authority. A consumer asking for the stronger property
must use `witness-epoch-transparency-verify`, which fails closed when the log,
certificate, or quorum is unavailable.

## Native And Linear Boundary

Frame `9016` has eight independently sabotaged rules:

- `epoch_transparency_handoff_is_verified` binds an adjacent frame-9015 summary;
- `epoch_transparency_log_is_reachable_and_signed` forbids local-only fallback;
- `epoch_transparency_quorum_is_verified` requires an exact `3/4` current summary;
- `epoch_transparency_operator_is_independent` separates operator, local, and four witness principals;
- `epoch_transparency_append_is_monotonic` requires one new leaf and a changed root;
- `epoch_transparency_proofs_are_verified` binds presented roots to recomputed roots;
- `epoch_transparency_leaf_binds_handoff` binds leaf and predecessor digests to the handoff;
- `epoch_transparency_latest_epoch_matches` rejects included-but-stale active epochs.

The verified handoff and checkpoint summaries are linear. Joining them consumes
both once and yields one `VerifiedEpochTransparency`; construction of its host
receipt is module-private. External receipt construction refuses with `E176`,
and reusing either authority token refuses with `E039`.

## Evidence Boundary

The executable PL/CS mechanism is the composition of a linear reconfiguration
receipt, a recomputed materialized Merkle proof, an external current-quorum
split-view witness, a crash-recoverable promotion order, and rule-level
necessity controls in the executable harness. This is a concrete research artifact, not a literature
priority claim. Comparison with Certificate Transparency, Trillian, CONIKS,
SUNDR, fork-linearizable storage, transparency overlays, and reconfiguration
logics requires a separate sourced related-work review.

## Falsification Conditions

- strong verify succeeds with no reachable log or only a local receipt;
- an operator-signed old or forked snapshot agrees with three current witnesses;
- a Merkle root is trusted without recomputing the returned leaves;
- a reordered, dropped, duplicated, or substituted handoff remains latest;
- an older included handoff is accepted as the active epoch;
- a two-step append advances by zero or more than one leaf;
- a crash after append creates a different retry leaf;
- fewer than three current witness statuses authorize a strong read;
- the operator shares the local production host or a witness principal without refusal;
- a report calls the mechanism freeze detection, availability, consensus, full recovery, two-dishonest safety, or cross-host custody based only on the local gate;
- replacing a named frame-9016 rule with `true` fails to admit its exact paired necessity control.
